					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-212269#post-1523586</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-212269/his-clockwork-servants#post-1523586</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 31 Jul 2012 08:49:17 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>tunedtoadeadchannel</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>304457</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Depends where you put the emphasis. When I wrote it, I emphasized the first syllable of &quot;broken&quot;. Adding a syllable to &quot;turn&quot; and de-emphasizing &quot;broken&quot; also works, I suppose, though I prefer to keep it in an active tense rather than passive, because I want to give the line a feeling of power.</p> <p>Same kinda dealie on the last line, only I disagree with your version way more; I used &quot;they are made to understand&quot; because from the CotBG's perspective, the mission is exactly that; remove the oppositions very <em>ability</em> to disagree. As far as meter, it's an eight count like the end line of each, though it splits differently. If you stress &quot;they&quot;, it flows okay.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-212269#post-1456475</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-212269/his-clockwork-servants#post-1456475</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 22 May 2012 18:16:59 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Aburr</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1299372</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Yeah, this is cute enough to get an upvote. The meter (meter?) on two of the rhymes looks slightly off to me, though I can't claim to know shit about that sort of thing and certainly might be wrong:</p> <p><em>&quot;What marvels are in His remaking!<br /> What wonders are in Her control!<br /> His Broken Gears turn forever<br /> restoring the penitent soul!&quot;</em></p> <p>I think it matches if you make &quot;turn&quot; into &quot;turning&quot;, and&#8230;</p> <p><em>&quot;We are His Clockwork Servants!<br /> We do the work of His hand!<br /> Those who oppose will forgive us<br /> when they are made to understand!&quot;</em></p> <p>Changing the last line to &quot;when they at last understand&quot; likewise makes this flow better in my head. Anyways, yes, I like it.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
